From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 23:00:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(servers): show reachable and compatible Bedrock servers
 correctly

The server list showed a Bedrock server that answered its status request
as incompatible, with "Target version: null". A server that did not
answer showed full green ping bars under "Can't connect to server".

Vanilla's server entry handles the ping result in two ways. An exception
from pingServer marks the entry unreachable. A completed ping runs
onPongResponse, which sets the state again by comparing ServerData.protocol
with the Java client protocol. The NetherNet status path set its own state
and then ran onPongResponse with a Bedrock protocol number on success and
the default Java number on failure, so vanilla inverted both results.

Query the HTTP NetherNet capability endpoint synchronously on vanilla's
ping thread, like vanilla's own blocking TCP connect, and throw on failure
so the entry becomes unreachable. Report the Java protocol for a server on
the supported Bedrock protocol and the server's own protocol otherwise.
Record Bedrock as the translating version for the ViaFabricPlus tooltip.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

